Index 36 is valid because the last element of an array containing 37 elements has index 36.

Global IDs 37, 38, and 39 are outside the valid range. They must not process array elements.

## 5. Race Conditions and Parallel Reduction

### 5.1. Task 4.1: Naive reduction kernel

The naive kernel attempts to add values from multiple GPU threads into one shared scalar location.

```python
@cuda.jit
def naive_sum_kernel(d_arr, d_total):
    idx = cuda.grid(1)

    if idx < d_arr.shape[0]:
        d_total[0] += d_arr[idx]
```

The problem is that multiple threads may read the same old value of `d_total[0]`, independently add their input values, and write the results back. Some updates can be lost.

This is called a race condition.

### 5.2. Correct atomic reduction

The atomic version uses `cuda.atomic.add`:

```python
@cuda.jit
def atomic_sum_kernel(d_arr, d_total):
    idx = cuda.grid(1)

    if idx < d_arr.shape[0]:
        cuda.atomic.add(d_total, 0, d_arr[idx])
```

An atomic addition ensures that each update to the shared scalar is performed without conflicting with another update to the same memory location.

